{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Lunar Strike</strong> is a single-player narrative adventure and exploration game set on the Moon\u2019s South Pole in the year 2119. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as a junior archivist sent to document humanity\u2019s final lunar colony. Your mission begins with scanning and preserving scientific, cultural, and personal records. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But when sabotage destabilizes the colony, the task shifts to survival under real lunar conditions: managing oxygen, power, and time while deciding what knowledge and memory must endure. Every choice shapes the archive \u2014 and the outcome of the colony itself.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3949580/extras/d288d8ee96e0409c0b77d995ef82b4c1.avif?t=1755719998\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3949580/extras_big/d288d8ee96e0409c0b77d995ef82b4c1.webp?t=1755719998 width=1560 height=878 /></span>Developed with ethical questions of legacy, memory, and responsibility at its heart, players will face increasingly difficult challenges to build and preserve the archive, with multiple outcomes driven by their decisions and values.<br><br><strong>Narrative adventure set on the Moon\u2019s South Pole (2119)</strong> \u2014 explore a colony on the edge of collapse.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>No combat</strong> \u2014 gameplay revolves around survival adventure, exploration, and preservation.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Archival scanning tools</strong> \u2014 recover, analyze, and prioritize data across cultural, scientific, and personal domains.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tactical survival mechanics</strong> \u2014 manage oxygen, suit energy, and habitat systems under lunar constraints.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Branching narrative outcomes</strong> \u2014 decisions on what to save or abandon reshape the colony\u2019s legacy.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Forensic reconstruction </strong> \u2014 analyse a crime scene from scanned artifacts.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Characters that challenge your perspective</strong> .</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Grounded in real science</strong> \u2014 environments, orbital mechanics, and survival systems are modeled on current lunar research.<br><br><br><br></p></li></ul>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3949580?t=1755719998","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3949580/b0fdb76bd05e293fed6cfd04836a5797c50f48bd/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1755719998","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3949580/b9a4482d6be723bc9e231211e7ed44faafd27639/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1755719998","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3949580/b9a4482d6be723bc9e231211e7ed44faafd27639/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1755719998","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Full controller support","id":28},{"description":"Save Anytime","id":79},{"description":"Stereo Sound","id":69},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"controller_support":"full","detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Lunar Strike</strong> is a single-player narrative adventure and exploration game set on the Moon\u2019s South Pole in the year 2119. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as a junior archivist sent to document humanity\u2019s final lunar colony. Your mission begins with scanning and preserving scientific, cultural, and personal records. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But when sabotage destabilizes the colony, the task shifts to survival under real lunar conditio